```java
public int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
    int left = 0;
    int right = arr.length - 1;
    while (left <= right) {
        int mid = (left + right) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == target) {
            return mid;
        } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
            left = mid + 1;
        } else {
            right = mid - 1;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

this one takes an array and a target value as input. it uses two pointers, left and right, to keep track of the current search interval. the algorithm repeatedly divides the search interval in half until it finds the target value or determines that it is not present. if the target value is found, the index at which it was found is returned. if the target value is not found, the function returns -1.

important bit: the input array must be sorted in ascending order for this binary search algorithm to work ^^
